        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-24T20:33:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This assumes that the structure size was increased in a compatible way. We have not such guarantees or rules when updating the panic_info struct right now.\n\nThe struct may be larger because some other struct in the union was increased, or it may have increased because we added another field at the beginning of the arch structure.\n\nBasically trying to reinterpret these bytes in the new structures is undefined since the RW does not know what the format was in RO.\n\nIf the struct size in memory doesn\u0027t match CONFIG_PANIC_DATA_SIZE, then we should not try to parse it. We should instead just display it in hex on the console or something like that. It is already included in feedback reports as binary data, so we can parse that binary data with the tool build from either RO or RW code.",
